notes: DSMZ 601 and NBRC 1183 describe artificial sea water prepared from marine aquarium
  salt mixtures without identifying a particular product. MicrO MICRO:0001715 defines
  the generic inorganic salts solution that mimics sea water, not one fixed formula.
  The spacing variant Artificial sea water therefore belongs to the existing generic
  Artificial seawater owner; no product-specific identity is selected. Specific aquarium
  product, batch formula and strength remain unknown; they are not prerequisites for
  this spelling-only association to the existing explicitly generic ontology sense.
  Provenance-only source text 'Artificial sea water' (case CM_NAME:e88d9dba7b6c89f143d72d69e57c72390ec19461c2bb1456f248e761559e41cd).
